 1145 "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(4,8,2).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ 8 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083796/assets/0589ebbdb2c14b93e1296b9e1f8b0caa0c3df49bff4c9fbb97e4c18102844ec1.png)\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $\\Pi$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overrightarrow{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot 4+4\\cdot (-4)|}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-4)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-2+24-16|}{\\sqrt{4+16+16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\,6\\,|}{\\sqrt{36}} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186119763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388029 13194139536190 true] [17592186119763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388036 13194139536190 true] [17592186119763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388064 13194139536190 true] [17592186119763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388071 13194139536190 true] [17592186119764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388043 13194139536190 true] [17592186119765 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388050 13194139536190 true] [17592186119765 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388057 13194139536190 true] [17592186119765 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388078 13194139536190 true] [17592186119765 1020 #edb/ref 17592186388085 13194139536190 true] [17592186388029 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388030 13194139536190 true] [17592186388029 1089 "q-129094" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388029 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536190 true] [17592186388029 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(1,2,-3)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}])\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]=0.$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388029 1113 #uuid "1ad8882e-4e17-5620-b084-21aafa42032d" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388029 1145 "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(1,-2,1).$ Then \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|0\\cdot (-2)+(-4)\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 2|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4+8|}{\\sqrt{4+1+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|4|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388031 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388032 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388033 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388034 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388035 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1041 "selection" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388033 13194139536190 true] [17592186388030 1110 #uuid "3cbf1f02-a404-5378-a26b-f2713a97b4a2" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388031 1034 "\\frac{9}{3}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388031 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388031 1111 #uuid "f2dfb090-8668-52ad-87bd-7b0c2cb7dc62" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388032 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388032 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388032 1111 #uuid "ce7dfdef-a6f6-53cf-91a1-51499188e0a5" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388033 1034 "\\frac{4}{3}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388033 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388033 1111 #uuid "2ca79318-c292-567b-b18d-294f042b379e" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388034 1034 "\\frac{5}{3}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388034 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388034 1111 #uuid "c423bea4-eabc-5c5c-8335-12e04762c48a" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388035 1034 "\\frac{7}{3}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388035 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388035 1111 #uuid "9e3905ae-e406-5602-8a76-21672e1b8986" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388036 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388037 13194139536190 true] [17592186388036 1089 "q-129098" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388036 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536190 true] [17592186388036 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-4,3,-1)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $(r-⟨6,-1,5⟩)\\cdot ⟨-1,2,-2⟩=0.$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388036 1113 #uuid "57b9ef22-fb1b-538b-ae87-f09c0b621f1b" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388036 1145 "Let's pick a point on the plane, for instance, $Q(6,-1,5).$ Then\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨6,-1,5⟩-⟨-4,3,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨10,-4,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAlso, from the equation of the plane, we get a normal vector $n=⟨-1,2,-2⟩.$\n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|10\\cdot (-1)+(-4)\\cdot 2+6\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-10-8-12|}{\\sqrt{1+4+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-30|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30}{3} \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388038 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388039 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388040 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388041 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388042 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1041 "selection" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388041 13194139536190 true] [17592186388037 1110 #uuid "e836f468-f33f-5437-852e-2bfa512d2628" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388038 1034 "12" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388038 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388038 1111 #uuid "6e2ca9a1-fb24-5712-925c-5959e12d4c2e" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388039 1034 "9" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388039 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388039 1111 #uuid "4019b38c-aa2b-5ec7-a820-42d26bea3bde" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388040 1034 "\\frac{25}{3}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388040 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388040 1111 #uuid "802b8e11-2584-5155-a4cd-2ebfe252af39" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388041 1034 "10" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388041 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388041 1111 #uuid "2f7c4579-cee8-5fb1-815b-20318945d169" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388042 1034 "\\frac{32}{3}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388042 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388042 1111 #uuid "b0c6e63e-b389-5e51-b321-fb6bce740b73" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388043 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388044 13194139536190 true] [17592186388043 1089 "q-129119" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388043 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536190 true] [17592186388043 1100 "Given that $Q(1,-3,7)$ lies on the plane $Π:r\\cdot ⟨6,3,-2⟩=-17$, find the shortest distance from $P(2,-6,2)$ to $Π.$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388043 1113 #uuid "b78702ba-d6e3-50bb-96e7-281310599418" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388043 1145 "First, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,-3,7⟩-⟨2,-6,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,3,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the equation of the plane, we get the normal vector $n=⟨6,3,-2⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|(-1)\\cdot 6+3\\cdot 3+5\\cdot (-2)|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-6+9-10|}{\\sqrt{36+9+4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-7|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{7} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388045 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388046 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388047 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388048 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388049 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1041 "selection" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388047 13194139536190 true] [17592186388044 1110 #uuid "575c10d3-5e8b-5ded-aacf-435058c1f6a4" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388045 1034 "3" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388045 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388045 1111 #uuid "6d34557c-9668-573a-b832-0e087b548a78" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388046 1034 "2" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388046 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388046 1111 #uuid "c8508785-7cce-5b15-a748-06f59d173d96" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388047 1034 "1" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388047 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388047 1111 #uuid "197ef296-f4e1-510f-a17f-7a953b342003" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388048 1034 "4" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388048 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388048 1111 #uuid "2875b1e3-3614-576a-98fe-8d853f1d9a86" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388049 1034 "5" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388049 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388049 1111 #uuid "ae7982c3-8b00-5fc8-86c3-9aa66b34bb45" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388050 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388051 13194139536190 true] [17592186388050 1089 "q-129158" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388050 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536190 true] [17592186388050 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,3,-4)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $6x+2y+3z=9.$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388050 1113 #uuid "e3db73ba-3f2a-5efa-9740-ea27b4704163" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388050 1145 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=0$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+2y+3z & =9 \\\\ 6(1)+2(0)+3z & =9 \\\\ 3z & =3 \\\\ z & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,0,1)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,0,1⟩-⟨-1,3,-4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,5⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨6,2,3⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot 6+(-3)\\cdot 2+5\\cdot 3|}{\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{2}^{2}+{3}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|12-6+15|}{\\sqrt{36+4+9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|21|}{\\sqrt{49}} \\\\  & =\\frac{21}{7} \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388052 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388053 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388054 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388055 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388056 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1041 "selection" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1104 #edb/ref 17592186388054 13194139536190 true] [17592186388051 1110 #uuid "975ae3ec-ee75-592b-af2a-76eb70da9777" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388052 1034 "\\frac{7}{2}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388052 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388052 1111 #uuid "e8eaacf8-bb02-5974-8bbc-0c424a836d11" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388053 1034 "\\frac{30}{7}" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388053 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388053 1111 #uuid "bebba3c6-ca59-5e2e-8a7c-51a59b84e7e4" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388054 1034 "3" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388054 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388054 1111 #uuid "87aadc4b-2eef-5b06-9aa0-aef0ec8b3955" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388055 1034 "2" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388055 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388055 1111 #uuid "09f05e42-531e-50ab-8024-b477c36efdc5" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388056 1034 "5" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388056 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536190 true] [17592186388056 1111 #uuid "05569caf-db27-5128-987f-36082784f425" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388057 1017 #edb/ref 17592186388058 13194139536190 true] [17592186388057 1089 "q-129165" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388057 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536190 true] [17592186388057 1100 "Find the shortest distance between the point $P(-1,4,-5)$ and the plane $Π$ with equation $-2x+2y+z=6.$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388057 1113 #uuid "64474450-57b0-5c05-b9ab-5a9f07006716" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388057 1145 "Let's start by picking a point on the plane. To do that, we simply substitute some concrete values for $x$ and $y$ into the equation and solve for $z.$ Let's choose $x=1$ and $y=1$ (though it doesn't really matter what values we choose). Solving for $z,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+2y+z & =6 \\\\ -2(1)+2(1)+z & =6 \\\\ z & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the point $Q(1,1,6)$ which lies on the plane.\n\nComputing $\\overset{\\to }{PQ},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨1,1,6⟩-⟨-1,4,-5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-3,11⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe also need a normal vector to the plane. For any Cartesian equation of a plane $ax+by+cz=d,$ the normal vector is $n=⟨a,b,c⟩.$ So, for the plane $Π,$ we have $n=⟨-2,2,1⟩.$ \n\nFinally, the shortest distance from the point $P$ to the plane $Π$ is the absolute value of the scalar projection of $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ onto the normal vector of the plane:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =|{\\text{comp}}_{n}\\,\\overset{\\to }{PQ}| \\\\  & =\\frac{|\\overset{\\to }{PQ}\\cdot n|}{|n|} \\\\  & =\\frac{|2\\cdot (-2)+(-3)\\cdot 2+11\\cdot 1|}{\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{2}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|-4-6+11|}{\\sqrt{4+4+1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{|1|}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388059 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388060 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388061 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388062 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1000 #edb/ref 17592186388063 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1041 "selection" 13194139536190 true] [17592186388058 1104 #ed